WEBVTT

00:00:00.180 --> 00:00:05.916
Welcome to LeafByte. This page loads seven megabytes of original images.

00:00:07.180 --> 00:00:13.156
LeafByte keeps the layout, and cuts image data to two hundred and four kilobytes.

00:00:14.180 --> 00:00:21.428
A second page shows the same approach, using ninety-one point seven percent less image data.

00:00:22.180 --> 00:00:29.812
Start with a folder of photographs. These twenty-six licensed images are processed right here, in your browser.

00:00:32.180 --> 00:00:40.532
Take a moment to compare the real output. This laptop photo becomes twenty kilobytes at eight hundred pixels wide.

00:00:42.180 --> 00:00:50.292
Across the batch, the median reduction is ninety-two point four percent, with images resized for the web.

00:00:52.180 --> 00:01:01.372
For climate context, the Sustainable Web Design model estimates carbon impact, using your traffic, caching, and hosting assumptions.

00:01:04.180 --> 00:01:12.508
For ten thousand hypothetical views, the first page models about eight to ten kilograms of carbon dioxide equivalent.

00:01:14.180 --> 00:01:21.044
Export optimized images, responsive markup, file sizes, and verification hashes.

00:01:22.180 --> 00:01:28.468
Explore the repository for measured bytes, visible choices, and clear assumptions.
